The failing test indicates a `ClassCastException` because the key (originally intended to be a String) is being processed or expected as another type (an Integer in this instance). This generally happens because the refactor did not ensure keys were consistently Strings or converted to Strings when stored.

To fix the bug, ensure that all keys used in the `map.put` operations are Strings, which would prevent ClassCastExceptions related to type misalignment of keys.

